    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0187" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/5–641</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-06">May 6, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>We have clear indication that Admiral [Nomura] is having to try to “sell” to his
                    Government (at least his Foreign Office) the project for an agreement between
                    Japan and the United States, to which project the John Doe associates have been
                    telling us that the Japanese controlling authorities (the backers of Colonel
                    [Itakuro]) are already committed in principle.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ornbeck</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
